<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eric IV of Denmark</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1216">1216</a>–<a href="/years/1250">1250</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Eric Ploughpenny</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eric IV, known as Eric Ploughpenny after a tax he levied on ploughs, was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> from 1241 to 1250. His reign was dominated by conflict with his brothers and the Church. In 1248 he granted Reval (Tallinn), then under Danish rule, the law of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lubeck">Lübeck</a>. He was murdered in 1250, probably at the instigation of his brother Abel, who succeeded him.</p></div>
